{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118068","id":3476898432,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7PPUKA","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118068","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118068.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118068.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118068","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118068/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118068/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118068/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/501dce76cd5c8df6e9c48cd6967ca2d5f389a686","number":118068,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix GDExtension ptrcall Ref<T> return refcount leak","user":{"login":"gtmacdonald","id":3230260,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzAyNjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3230260?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtmacdonald","html_url":"https://github.com/gtmacdonald","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtmacdonald/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtmacdonald/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtmacdonald/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtmacdonald/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtmacdonald/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtmacdonald/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtmacdonald/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtmacdonald/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtmacdonald/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\r\n\r\nGDExtension `object_method_bind_ptrcall` leaks one reference on every call to a method that returns `Ref<T>` (e.g. `get_mesh()`, `get_material()`, `get_texture()`, `get_shader()`). The leaked reference prevents the `RefCounted` object from ever being freed, causing RID leaks reported at shutdown.\r\n\r\nThis affects **all GDExtension bindings** that use ptrcall — godot-zig, godot-rust/gdext, godot-cpp, etc.\r\n\r\n## Root Cause\r\n\r\n`PtrToArg<Ref<T>>::encode` (in `core/variant/method_ptrcall.h:287`) treats the return buffer as a `Ref<T>` and assigns into it via `Ref<T>::operator=`, which calls `reference()` to increment the refcount.\r\n\r\n- **Internal C++ callers** allocate a `Ref<T>` on the stack and pass its address. The `Ref<T>` destructor eventually calls `unreference()`, balancing the increment. ✅\r\n- **GDExtension callers** provide a raw `Object**` buffer (8 bytes initialized to null) with no destructor. The `encode` writes into it, incrementing the refcount, but nothing ever decrements it. The GDExtension binding reads the raw `Object*` pointer and has no mechanism to know a `Ref<T>` was involved. ❌\r\n\r\nEvery ptrcall to a method returning `Ref<T>` permanently increments the refcount by 1.\r\n\r\n## Fix\r\n\r\nAfter `mb->ptrcall()`, detect `Ref<T>` returns (return type is `Variant::OBJECT` and `!is_return_type_raw_object_ptr()`) and call `unreference()` on the returned object to compensate. The GDExtension caller receives a borrowed pointer with the correct refcount — matching GDScript semantics.\r\n\r\n## Reproduction\r\n\r\n**Minimal reproduction using godot-zig** (same issue applies to any GDExtension binding using ptrcall):\r\n\r\n1. Create a GDExtension `MeshInstance3D` subclass that:\r\n   - Creates an `ArrayMesh` via `ArrayMesh::init()`\r\n   - Adds a surface via `variantCall(\"add_surface_from_arrays\", ...)`\r\n   - Calls `setMesh()` via ptrcall\r\n   - Calls `getMesh()` via ptrcall (this is the leak trigger)\r\n2. Create multiple instances, `queue_free` them in cycles, then quit\r\n3. Observe `ERROR: N RID allocations of type 'Mesh' were leaked at exit` and `ObjectDB instances leaked`\r\n\r\n## Related Issues\r\n\r\n- #73577 — RID leaks at exit with dynamic meshes (partially explained by this bug)\r\n- #80140 — Mesh RID leaks on scene change\r\n- #69910 — RID leak warnings at shutdown\r\n- godot-rust/gdext#108 — `get_mesh()` ptrcall return leaks a reference (identified the symptom)\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n\r\n- Verified zero RID leaks with the fix using both a minimal reproduction scene and a full tile rendering system (~3,452 dynamically created `ArrayMesh` instances with visual mode cycling)\r\n- The fix only affects the GDExtension ptrcall path — internal C++ ptrcall semantics are unchanged\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-04-01T12:10:29Z","updated_at":"2026-04-01T12:33:44Z","closed_at":"2026-04-01T12:22:55Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"27d21f7e6b186950299b3100c6be1953e10bccf4","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"gtmacdonald:fix/gdextension-ptrcall-ref-leak","ref":"fix/gdextension-ptrcall-ref-leak","repo":{"id":1058455265,"node_id":"R_kgDOPxa-4Q","name":"godot","full_name":"gtmacdonald/godot","owner":{"login":"gtmacdonald","id":3230260,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzAyNjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3230260?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtmacdonald","html_url":"https://github.com/gtmacdonald","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtmacdonald/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gtmacdonald/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/use